{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5f3799cd",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 02 - K-Means on a Subsample  (Stage 2)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Purpose.** Fit `MiniBatchKMeans` on a 200k subsample of `complete`\n",
    "trajectories for several `k`, evaluate each `k` (inertia, silhouette, cluster\n",
    "sizes, maps), and pickle every model so the best `k` can be chosen later.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Input.** `data/features.parquet`  (Stage 1).\n",
    "**Output.** `data/kmeans_models/kmeans_k*.pkl`, evaluation plots in `figures/`.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Feature handling.** Positions are *not* standardised (absolute geography\n",
    "matters). With `config.FEATURE_SPACE = \"xyz\"` (default) each day-50 / day-100\n",
    "position is embedded on the unit sphere as Cartesian `(x, y, z)` inside\n",
    "`pipeline.build_feature_matrix`, giving a 6-D vector. Euclidean distance there is\n",
    "the chord -- a monotonic function of the great-circle (haversine) distance -- so\n",
    "plain k-means clusters by true spherical distance and the centroids\n",
    "(re-projected to lat/lon by `pipeline.centroids_to_degrees`) are proper spherical\n",
    "centroids. The `z` here is the polar geometry axis, **not** ocean depth. Set\n",
    "`FEATURE_SPACE = \"cosine\"` for the legacy near-equator approximation."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a45a5822",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import sys, os\n",
    "sys.path.insert(0, os.path.abspath(\"..\"))   # project root: config.py, pipeline.py\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import config as C\n",
    "import pipeline as P\n",
    "print(\"project root:\", C.PROJECT_ROOT)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "db9298d3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2.1  Load features and take a reproducible 200k subsample"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "73aeb9ea",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "features = pd.read_parquet(C.FEATURES_FILE)\n",
    "complete = features[features.status == \"complete\"]\n",
    "n_sub = min(C.N_SUB, len(complete))\n",
    "sub = complete.sample(n=n_sub, random_state=C.RANDOM_STATE)\n",
    "X_sub = P.build_feature_matrix(sub)\n",
    "print(f\"complete: {len(complete):,}  ->  subsample: {X_sub.shape}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7613c331",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2.2  Fit MiniBatchKMeans for each k and evaluate"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "5399f450",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pickle, time\n",
    "from sklearn.cluster import MiniBatchKMeans\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import silhouette_score\n",
    "\n",
    "results = []\n",
    "for k in C.K_LIST:\n",
    "    t0 = time.time()\n",
    "    km = MiniBatchKMeans(n_clusters=k, random_state=C.RANDOM_STATE,\n",
    "                         batch_size=10000, n_init=10, max_iter=300)\n",
    "    labels = km.fit_predict(X_sub)\n",
    "    sil = silhouette_score(X_sub, labels, sample_size=C.SILHOUETTE_SAMPLE,\n",
    "                           random_state=C.RANDOM_STATE)\n",
    "    sizes = np.bincount(labels, minlength=k)\n",
    "    with open(C.MODELS_DIR / f\"kmeans_k{k}.pkl\", \"wb\") as f:\n",
    "        pickle.dump(km, f)\n",
    "    results.append(dict(k=k, inertia=km.inertia_, silhouette=sil,\n",
    "                        min_size=sizes.min(), max_size=sizes.max()))\n",
    "    print(f\"k={k:2d}  inertia={km.inertia_:.1f}  silhouette={sil:.3f}  \"\n",
    "          f\"sizes[{sizes.min()}..{sizes.max()}]  ({time.time()-t0:.1f}s)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "res = pd.DataFrame(results)\n",
    "res"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "aaaf4ebb",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2.3  Elbow and silhouette plots"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "9a4df041",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "fig, (a1, a2) = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(11, 4))\n",
    "a1.plot(res.k, res.inertia, \"o-\"); a1.set_xlabel(\"k\"); a1.set_ylabel(\"inertia\")\n",
    "a1.set_title(\"Elbow plot\")\n",
    "a2.plot(res.k, res.silhouette, \"o-\"); a2.set_xlabel(\"k\")\n",
    "a2.set_ylabel(\"silhouette\"); a2.set_title(\"Silhouette vs k\")\n",
    "fig.tight_layout()\n",
    "fig.savefig(C.FIG_DIR / \"elbow_plot.png\", dpi=130)\n",
    "fig.savefig(C.FIG_DIR / \"silhouette_plot.png\", dpi=130)\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "aeb13bf3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2.4  Cluster maps for each k\n",
    "\n",
    "For every `k`, colour the subsample's day-50 (dots) and day-100 (x) positions by\n",
    "cluster label so the spatial structure can be judged by eye."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "8cc9de75",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pickle\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, len(C.K_LIST), figsize=(4*len(C.K_LIST), 4), squeeze=False)\n",
    "for ax, k in zip(axes[0], C.K_LIST):\n",
    "    with open(C.MODELS_DIR / f\"kmeans_k{k}.pkl\", \"rb\") as f:\n",
    "        km = pickle.load(f)\n",
    "    lab = km.predict(X_sub)\n",
    "    ax.scatter(sub.lon_50, sub.lat_50, c=lab, s=2, cmap=\"tab20\", alpha=.4)\n",
    "    ax.scatter(sub.lon_100, sub.lat_100, c=lab, s=2, cmap=\"tab20\", marker=\"x\", alpha=.4)\n",
    "    ax.set_title(f\"k={k}\"); ax.set_xlabel(\"lon\"); ax.set_ylabel(\"lat\")\n",
    "fig.tight_layout()\n",
    "fig.savefig(C.FIG_DIR / \"cluster_maps_by_k.png\", dpi=120)\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "fccdb55c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2.5  Suggested cluster groupings (over-resolve, then merge)\n",
    "\n",
    "We are **not** looking for a single \"optimal\" k. Instead pick a fairly high k\n",
    "(e.g. 20-25) so the structure is over-resolved into many fine clusters, then\n",
    "merge the fine clusters that represent the *same* physical pathway into a few\n",
    "named groups.\n",
    "\n",
    "The dendrogram below performs a Ward hierarchical clustering on the chosen\n",
    "model's centroids: clusters that join low down are spatially similar and are\n",
    "good candidates to merge. `pipeline.suggest_groups` cuts that tree into\n",
    "`n_groups` and returns a `{raw_cluster: group}` map you can paste into\n",
    "`config.GROUP_MAP` (and then refine by eye)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "0723bce7",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pickle\n",
    "from scipy.cluster.hierarchy import dendrogram\n",
    "\n",
    "INSPECT_K = 20     # the k you want to take forward and group\n",
    "N_GROUPS  = 6      # how many merged pathway groups you want to end up with\n",
    "\n",
    "with open(C.MODELS_DIR / f\"kmeans_k{INSPECT_K}.pkl\", \"rb\") as f:\n",
    "    km_i = pickle.load(f)\n",
    "cent_deg = P.centroids_to_degrees(km_i.cluster_centers_)   # for readable labels\n",
    "group_map, Z = P.suggest_groups(km_i.cluster_centers_, N_GROUPS)\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(11, 4))\n",
    "dendrogram(Z, labels=[f\"{c}\" for c in range(INSPECT_K)], ax=ax,\n",
    "           color_threshold=Z[-(N_GROUPS-1), 2])\n",
    "ax.set_title(f\"Centroid dendrogram (k={INSPECT_K}); cut -> {N_GROUPS} groups\")\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel(\"raw cluster id\"); ax.set_ylabel(\"Ward distance\")\n",
    "fig.savefig(C.FIG_DIR / f\"centroid_dendrogram_k{INSPECT_K}.png\", dpi=130, bbox_inches=\"tight\")\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Suggested GROUP_MAP (paste into config.py, then refine):\")\n",
    "print(\"GROUP_MAP =\", group_map)\n",
    "for g in sorted(set(group_map.values())):\n",
    "    members = [c for c, gg in group_map.items() if gg == g]\n",
    "    print(f\"  group {g}: clusters {members}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "849136b6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2.6  Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "Models for every k are pickled in `data/kmeans_models/`. Decide:\n",
    "1. which **k** to carry forward (set `BEST_K` in notebooks 03 & 04), and\n",
    "2. (optionally) the **GROUP_MAP** that merges fine clusters into pathway groups\n",
    "   (paste into `config.py`).\n",
    "\n",
    "If you set `GROUP_MAP`, notebooks 03 and 04 will additionally produce a\n",
    "`cluster_group` column and group-level figures; if you leave it empty they fall\n",
    "back to the raw clusters."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "851647d6",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"models saved:\", sorted(p.name for p in C.MODELS_DIR.glob('kmeans_k*.pkl')))\n",
    "print(res.to_string(index=False))"
   ]
  }
 ],
